From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000052 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@fxgam.es>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:55:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Reject oversized texel views before Metal (STEAMAC-9E/79)

The captured Metal assertion names width 536346624, over its 268435456
capacity. MoltenVK advertises only 67108864 texels, but both explicit and
VK_WHOLE_SIZE views bypassed that limit and were narrowed to uint32_t
before the lazy Metal constructor, which aborts instead of returning nil.

Validate the resolved texel count before narrowing. Reject an oversized
view at creation instead of aborting the VM during descriptor update.
Keep legal maximum-size views and partial final texels with WHOLE_SIZE.

texel_limits.c reproduces the assertion on M1 Max, using an R8 WHOLE_SIZE
view over a 512 MiB buffer at offset 524288 (the original format/range was
not captured). Explicit and WHOLE_SIZE limit+1 views must fail; boundary
and partial controls must still update descriptors successfully.
---
diff --git a/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKBuffer.mm b/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKBuffer.mm
index 043ad07..1817ad0 100644
--- a/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKBuffer.mm
+++ b/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKBuffer.mm
@@ -353,6 +353,17 @@ static VkDeviceSize getTextureBufferOffsetMask(const VkPhysicalDeviceTexelBuffer
     VkDeviceSize byteCount = pCreateInfo->range;
     if (byteCount == VK_WHOLE_SIZE) { byteCount = _buffer->getByteCount() - pCreateInfo->offset; }    // Remaining bytes in buffer
     size_t blockCount = byteCount / bytesPerBlock;
+	// Validate in 64 bits, before narrowing the width or lazily constructing a Metal
+	// texture. VK_WHOLE_SIZE is subject to maxTexelBufferElements too (VUID 04059).
+	// Metal aborts, rather than returning nil, for unrepresentable texture widths.
+	uint32_t maxElements = getDeviceProperties().limits.maxTexelBufferElements;
+	if (blockCount > maxElements) {
+		setConfigurationResult(reportError(VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY,
+										   "vkCreateBufferView(): Format %d, offset %llu, range %llu resolves to %zu texels, exceeding maxTexelBufferElements %u.",
+										   pCreateInfo->format, pCreateInfo->offset, pCreateInfo->range,
+										   blockCount, maxElements));
+		return;
+	}
 
 	_textureSize.width = uint32_t(blockCount * fmtBlockSize.width);
     _textureSize.height = 1;
